@bananiceee/dsh-status-bar README · Self-hosted Web / CLI：```sh
dsh plugin --profile web add @bananiceee/dsh-status-bar@0.3.1
```

@bananiceee/dsh-status-bar README · GitHub release; handy when git access to the repo is awkward)：dsh plugin --profile desktop add https://github.com/Starlight-bananice/dsh-status-bar/releases/download/v0.3.1/bananiceee-dsh-status-bar-0.3.1.tgz
```

> **Note:** pnpm 11 enforces a 24 h `minimumReleaseAge` for freshly published packages — if a same-day release is rejected, append `--config.minimumReleaseAge=0` to the `dsh plugin add` command.

@bananiceee/dsh-status-bar README · "Already up to date" and keeps the old build. Upgrade with a re-add:：dsh plugin --profile desktop remove @bananiceee/dsh-status-bar
dsh plugin --profile desktop add github:Starlight-bananice/dsh-status-bar#v0.3.1
```

@bananiceee/dsh-status-bar README · Disable：- **Switch to the native bar** — tick **Use native status bar** in Settings → Status Bar or the gear menu. The plugin releases both dock entries immediately and DSH's built-in bar (including its context meter) returns; untick to restore the plugin bar.
- **Hide the plugin bar only** — the client master switch (Settings → Status Bar, or the gear menu in the composer) turns the plugin bar off instantly; the host projections and the usage ledger keep running.
- **Stop the plugin entirely** — disable it on the in-app **Plugins** page (or remove it from the profile's `bundles` list); re-enabling restores it.
